Z||000019||Nashco||09-07-2001||04:54 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever3000:<BR><B>A nice Mustang will never get dis'd.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I laughed at this comment.  I go to Kettering University (formerly known as GM Institute) and pretty much every Ford owner, especially mustang owners, gets flack daily.  Outside of school I know a lot of people that don't like lots of Mustangs.<P>Personally, I like the late 60s/early 70s Mach 1s, and the last of the fox body mustang 5.0s, I think the rest are pretty much a waste of time.  Seriously, every Bob and Jane has one...I like to be part of a smaller crowd, if any crowd at all (thus my weird choice of cars).<P>I love DMCs, just because they have the stainless bodies...what many companies wish they could do.  Shelby took a step into the unknown with all-aluminum bodies, as did DMC with the stainless.  If they had a more technologically advanced drivetrain, I would really like them.  But, there are lots of conversions out there (including a N* kit)..and drivetrain is much easier to change than body panel metals!<P>Good luck...<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>||||reg||1
